  "description": "The meme promotes historical amnesia by suggesting that colonialism should be forgotten, which trivializes the lasting impacts of colonial exploitation, cultural erasure, and political subjugation. This normalization of forgetting can perpetuate inequality and injustice, particularly for communities still grappling with colonial legacies. The juxtaposition of a handshake (symbolizing reconciliation) with the dismissive text creates a morally ambiguous and potentially harmful message that undermines historical accountability and justice.",
